# fleet — scheduled maintenance.
#   crontab -e   and paste, adjusting the path.
#
# cron runs with a minimal environment, so PATH and the repo location must be explicit.
# Credentials come from <repo>/.env, which bin/fleet sources itself.

PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
FLEET_ROOT=/home/you/vpncascade

# Optional: where failures get shouted. Reads the message on stdin.
#   ntfy:     FLEET_NOTIFY_CMD=curl -s -d @- ntfy.sh/your-private-topic
#   telegram: FLEET_NOTIFY_CMD=curl -s -X POST -d chat_id=$CHAT -d text="$(cat)" https://api.telegram.org/bot$TOKEN/sendMessage
#   mail:     FLEET_NOTIFY_CMD=mail -s "fleet alert" you@example.com
# FLEET_NOTIFY_CMD=curl -s -d @- ntfy.sh/your-private-topic

# ── every 15 min: health, replace anything blocked from Russia, refill the pool ──
# This is the one that matters. An exit whose whole IP range gets blacklisted from
# Russia is dead to you immediately, not at its scheduled rotation.
*/15 * * * *  $FLEET_ROOT/cron/fleet-cron.sh cron

# ── hourly: destroy orphans and top up self-expiring nodes ──────────────────────
# `cron` already does this, but a separate cheap pass means a stuck rotation does
# not also stop you reclaiming a server you are paying for.
17 * * * *    $FLEET_ROOT/cron/fleet-cron.sh reap

# ── daily at 04:22: force a rotation even if nothing has aged out ───────────────
# A jittered minute, not :00 — a fleet that churns on the hour is itself a pattern.
22 4 * * *    $FLEET_ROOT/cron/fleet-cron.sh rotate

# ── weekly report ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 30 9 * * 1  $FLEET_ROOT/cron/fleet-cron.sh status


# ══ systemd alternative (better: proper logs, RandomizedDelaySec jitter) ════════
#
# /etc/systemd/system/fleet.service
#   [Unit]
#   Description=fleet maintenance
#   [Service]
#   Type=oneshot
#   User=you
#   WorkingDirectory=/home/you/vpncascade
#   ExecStart=/home/you/vpncascade/cron/fleet-cron.sh cron
#
# /etc/systemd/system/fleet.timer
#   [Unit]
#   Description=fleet maintenance every 15 minutes
#   [Timer]
#   OnCalendar=*:0/15
#   RandomizedDelaySec=180
#   Persistent=true
#   [Install]
#   WantedBy=timers.target
#
#   systemctl enable --now fleet.timer
#
# RandomizedDelaySec is worth having: it stops every rotation landing on the same
# wall-clock minute, which is the kind of regularity that makes a fleet easy to
# correlate across providers.
